          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "GREAT GADDESDEN        LEIGHTON BUZZARD ROAD(A4146) TL 0310                                         (West side)                                         Water End 10/108                                  Waterside Cottage - GV                                     II House. Late C17 or early C18. Roughcast with steep old red tile roofs. A 2-storeys,  2-cells, end-chimney plan house facing E with off-centre plank entrance door into N room, and external gable chimneys each of 2 flues, the N chimney being later. 2 windows to each floor and large gabled rustic porch. 3-light casement windows of C19 type with flush frames and square heads but ground floor S window of C18 type under segmental arch, flush with rectangular leaded panes and wrought iron central casement. Single-storey N extension with steep old tile roof partly roughcast but N part of dark weatherboarding. Formerly called Fishery Cottage. Listing NGR: TL0362510508"
    }
  ],
